~
The algorithm also sets up a set of bins, but it blurs each point using a bell-shaped burring function.  So a fraction of each point lands in each bin.  The net result is a smoother plot.   (Blurring each point is a bit better than smoothing the PDF's histogram, since it blurs from the location of each original point within the bin -- however it is more computationally intensive than just blurring the histogram.Author: Dale Rice~
