 nBins : positive = 100 )Title: Kernel Dens EstDescription: A kernel density estimator.  Returns a smooth PDF plot of x, optionally using a given kernel width.~
~
Typical usage:~
~
Kernel_Dens_Est( X )~
~
Or, to select your own kernel width (in units of X):~
~
Kernel_Dens_Est( X, width: 1.0 )~
~
To apply to a data set (other than a Monte-Carlo dervied set),  where the data is indexed by J:~
~
Kernel_Dens_est( data, I : J )~
~
You can also specify nBins to increase or decrease the number of bins in the resulting plot for more detail in the graph (with increased or decreased computational expense).Definition: var range := max(Z,I) - min(Z,I);~
if IsNotSpecified(width) then width:=range/50;~
index X := Sequence(min(Z,I),max(Z,I),range/nBins);~
Normalize(Sum( exp( -((Z-X)/width)^2 ), I), X)Nodelocation: 448,64,1Nodesize: 48,24Windstate: 2,489,171,547,842Paramnames: z,width,I,nBinsVariable A_kernel_density_estTitle: A kernel density estimatorDefinition: Kernel_dens_est(Analytica_s_pdf_plot)Nodelocation: 480,152,1Nodesize: 48,31Valuestate: 2,71,440,525,443,1,MIDMReformval: [Sys_localindex('X'),Undefined]{!40000|Att_resultslicestate: [Run,10,Sys_localindex('X'),1]}Close Kernel_density_estim